   "role": "mechanism",
   "level": "L3",
   "content": {
    "text": "Goods made by Chinese contractors for foreign firms are recorded as exports on delivery and as imports when resold in China at a higher price, creating a recorded goods deficit even though the goods never leave China.",
    "label": null,
    "explicit": true,
    "reason": "Recording transactions by residency rather than border crossing can create trade flows that never physically occur."
   },
   "source": {
